  "text": "The Tuatha Dé Danann are a magical race in Irish mythology. The Book of Invasions calls them the penultimate wave, distant kin of the people of Nemed. They beat the monstrous Fomorians and the Fir Bolg to win the land, and held Ireland for nearly three thousand years. Their name comes from the goddess Danu, so some call them Fir Dea, men of the goddess. They count Brigit, Eriu, the war goddesses Badb and Macha, the Dagda, Manannan Mac Lir, Dian Cecht, and Lugh. When the Milesians came, a treaty split the land: they took the surface, while the Tuatha Dé took the misty islands, the lake bottoms, and the fairy mounds. They became the immortal fairy people, yet they never left Ireland.",
